Chapter: RvParamBind

  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Does the body of a two-parameter function resolve each parameter name to
 the register the prologue bound it to? Nothing here recurses, matches, or
 tail-calls. Each function ignores one parameter and returns the other, so
 the answer names which register the body actually read.

 take-first 1 2 must be 1. take-second 1 2 must be 2. If the two answers
 are exchanged, the body's name-to-register mapping disagrees with the
 prologue and every other symptom in this area is downstream of that.

 The three-parameter case is here because a swap of two adjacent bindings
 and a full reversal of the list are different defects with the same
 signature at arity two.

Section: Probes

  take-first : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  take-first (a) (b) = a

  take-second : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  take-second (a) (b) = b

  of-three-first : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  of-three-first (a) (b) (c) = a

  of-three-mid : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  of-three-mid (a) (b) (c) = b

  of-three-last : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  of-three-last (a) (b) (c) = c

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni ("first: " & show (take-first 1 2))
   print-line-uni ("second: " & show (take-second 1 2))
   print-line-uni ("of3-first: " & show (of-three-first 1 2 3))
   print-line-uni ("of3-mid: " & show (of-three-mid 1 2 3))
   print-line-uni ("of3-last: " & show (of-three-last 1 2 3))
  end
